n  thank you spanjan  there's a second question in this regard  so um if and i don't know if that was  the case for you maybe carlotta have you  considered to use the flow rate of the  water also to normalize have you used  that or did you go with pmmov right away  yes so  we we  use the ppmov also to  our in control for  for for  uh  to see in order to see if there was a  dilution of the sample maybe  uh caused by the rain as uh also subian  said  so yeah we are we are planning also to  quantify the ppmov  and to use for normalization of the data  yeah thank you i know that many groups  are doing it this way  as well so thank you  there's one question if there is an  available method like a control for the  extraction step  i know that  both of you have done some testing  uh with spikes  while implementation does one of you  want to comment on that maybe  yeah i can go first yeah so for  the  matrix spike  so the way we uh  dealt with it is um  there was no consensus uh like um  what on what virus to use  and we have  tested for  uh  comparative analysis uh  coronaviruses human coronaviruses oc43  and 229e and so has carlota used some of  the coronaviruses  but uh due to like challenges of  culturing maintaining and using that as  a  for a starter lab we have mostly used  ms2  and for most purposes it serves serves  uh the need  so  like  like but it is entirely up to the  uh user on what uh uh best to use uh  yeah because  different people are using different uh  meditation then  in the ring trials that we've taken part  in  all ring trials were  either width  spiked they were either spiked with a  coronavirus  from the  organizer the ring trial organizer and  they had also asked us to spike  with  any other uh  matrix spike that we are using in the  lab  um  and  so  there are publications on  some there's some guidance on what to  use  thank you  i see that we are up the hour now thank  you very much i think we have to  finish this session  thank you very much t